WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.180
Take a square of card, thirty
centimetres along each side.

2
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:10.050
Cut an equal square from each corner, then
fold up the flaps to make an open box.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.300
Tiny squares give a flat tray.

4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.170
Huge ones give a tall, thin box.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.950
Both hold very little.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.090
So somewhere in between
there's a best cut.

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.690
How big should the corner squares be?

8
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.670
In this mission, you'll write the
volume in terms of one variable:

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.370
V equals x times thirty
minus two x, all squared.

10
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.940
You'll look for where
the graph of V is flat,

11
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:35.830
where the gradient is zero.

12
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:39.970
And the second derivative will tell you
whether it's a maximum or a minimum.

13
00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.550
Your mission: find the corner
cut that holds the most.
